  "notes": ["Each channel independently forks from the exact original normal startup. One-unit checks and commits, then single refill visits, do not establish any move release.","The original rate helper produces carry-in base 1 or 1.5 for a declared zero/nonzero +0x6FC. The actual refill wrapper consumes step 1 or 15.","Each inhibit-bit control holds its channel and still allows the other one. Uninitialized channel 1 stays masked.","For 0103/010A, checkpoint 0 declares clock 17; 1 is refill, 2 is debit, 3 is another refill, and 4 is a direct return call without a gameplay trigger.","The other timeline checkpoints are isolated wrapper visits. On 0800 the two observed debits have one ordinary refill visit between them.","The zero-limit mode-1 control checks that negative stock cannot pass a one-unit check or debit. No negative stock is admitted into the native domain.","No complete actor scheduling, gameplay return trigger, user input, wall-clock duration or native change is qualified."],
